.page top 1 watch the processes that use the most CPU

# SYNOPSIS
*top* [*-b*] [*-n* _COUNT_] [*-d* _SECONDS_]

# DESCRIPTION
`top` shows a live table of processes, busiest first: id, user, state, virtual and resident size, CPU share since the last refresh, and name. A line above it shows the uptime, the process count and the memory in use. The display is refreshed every two seconds; press `q` to leave.

When standard input is not a terminal `top` runs in batch mode.

# OPTIONS
@ *-b*
    Batch mode: print each table in turn without clearing the screen or reading keys.
@ *-n* _COUNT_
    Stop after _COUNT_ refreshes.
@ *-d* _SECONDS_
    Seconds between refreshes (fractions allowed). The default is 2.

# EXAMPLES
    top
    top -b -n 1

# SEE ALSO
ps(1), uptime(1), free(1)
